1.  Add a `selected` property to the `IOURequestStepParticipants.tsx` component to ensure that the participant is correctly identified.
2. Modify the `getParticipantsOption` function in `OptionsListUtils.ts` to use the `login` property to create a display name, even if the user is not in the `personalDetails` list.
3.  Ensure that the `avatar` is correctly set to the `FallbackAvatar` when the user's details are not available.

First, I will modify `src/pages/iou/request/step/IOURequestStepParticipants.tsx` to add the `selected` property. I will look for the `addParticipant` function and modify the `participants` array to include the `selected` property.

